Most pros and cons guides for wedding rentals list only pros, dressed up as a balanced comparison. Renting furniture, decor and catering are not trades Malaga Event Gear (MEG) works in, so this page stays inside the one slice we actually supply, the [Wedding Pack's](/packages/wedding/) sound, lighting, microphones and technician, and states the real limits alongside the real advantages, without softening either one. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) costs 650 euros ex VAT for up to 80 guests and includes a live technician who stays on site throughout the event. The real advantages are professional brand name gear, that technician, and flat transparent pricing with delivery and teardown included. The real limits are just as concrete: two fixed guest count tiers with no in between sizing, no self pickup option ever, no walk in showroom, and fixed prices with no negotiation. Both sides are stated plainly below, not hedged into each other.

## Key Highlights

---

- Real pros: professional Audix, QSC and Martin gear you would not buy for one event, a live technician included on the Wedding Pack, and flat pricing with delivery and teardown built in.
- Real cons: only two guest count tiers, delivery only with no self pickup, no showroom to test gear beforehand, and fixed prices with no negotiation.
- Renting a PA, mics and lighting for one wedding almost always beats buying: the equipment sits unused afterward with nowhere built in to store it.
- Hiring a full production company instead of an AV package like ours is a real, more expensive alternative most weddings do not need.

## The Real Pros of Renting Wedding AV

Renting the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) instead of assembling sound and lighting yourself brings a handful of concrete advantages that hold up to scrutiny.

**Professional, brand name gear.** MEG works with Audix, QSC and Martin, professional grade audio and lighting brands used across the live event industry, not consumer equipment bought for a single day and never touched again.

**A live technician who adjusts through the day.** The Wedding Pack includes on site technical control and engineering support throughout the event, someone who tunes the PA for vows, then for speeches, then for dancing, as the day actually moves. Most couples would never hire and manage that role themselves for a one time event.

**Flat, transparent pricing.** 650 euros ex VAT covers transport, professional setup and cabling, and post event teardown and pickup, in one published number rather than a quote assembled from separate delivery, setup and collection line items.

**No storage or maintenance burden afterward.** Once the technician packs up, the gear leaves with them. There is no PA system taking up a closet, no LED strings to coil and store, no equipment to maintain for an event that already happened.

<InlineCTA />

## The Real Cons, Stated Plainly

These are genuine limits, not softened caveats. If any of them matters more to your wedding than the advantages above, that is worth knowing before you book.

**Only two guest count tiers.** The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) covers up to 50 guests and the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) covers up to 80. There is no in between sizing and no per guest customization. A wedding of 65 guests still books the 80 guest package at the 80 guest price.

**Delivery only, no self pickup, ever.** Every system arrives on MEG's own transport and gets installed by our crew. A cost conscious couple who would rather collect the gear themselves and skip a delivery fee does not have that option with us.

**No walk in showroom.** You cannot audition the PA, test the wireless microphones, or see the fairy lighting in person before booking. What you get is described on the package page and confirmed at the quote stage, not tried on beforehand.

**Fixed prices, no negotiation.** MEG does not negotiate, price match, or discount for a weekday or off season date. Our [tips for reducing wedding rental costs](/blog/tips-for-reducing-wedding-rental-costs/) guide covers the one real lever that does exist, choosing the right package for your guest count, in more depth.

**A real minimum notice and a real distance threshold.** Services must be booked at least 24 hours in advance, so this is not a same day option. Book a wedding in Granada or another out of province destination and the total needs to exceed 400 euros to cover the travel, a genuine logistical constraint, not an abstract policy line.

## Eco Pack or Wedding Pack: What the Technician Actually Changes

| | Eco Pack | Wedding Pack |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guest count | Up to 50 | Up to 80 |
| Technician on site | No, self run after setup | Yes, throughout the event |
| Lighting | RGBW LED spotlights | Fairy lights and warm LED strings |
| Price (ex VAT) | 290 euros | 650 euros |

The Eco Pack is delivered, installed and tested by our crew, then left running unattended for the rest of the event, a real con if something needs adjusting mid reception and a real pro if you simply do not need anyone managing it. The Wedding Pack's technician is what the extra 360 euros buys: someone present to shift the sound from ceremony to speeches to dancing. Neither is the objectively better choice. It depends on your guest count and how much you want managed for you.

