## Renting vs Buying Your Own Rig for One Wedding

Buying a PA system, wireless microphones and a lighting rig outright for a single wedding rarely makes sense for anyone who is not already in the event industry. The capital cost alone, professional gear like this is a real investment, not a one time souvenir purchase, is hard to justify for equipment used once, and few couples have a realistic plan for where it goes afterward. Renting the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) trades that capital cost and storage problem for a single flat fee and someone else's problem to store and maintain the gear.

## Renting AV vs Hiring a Full Production Company

A full production company is a real alternative most general wedding rental guides never mention, because they compare rental categories, not services. A production company typically brings a larger team, custom staging, and a fully bespoke technical design, and charges accordingly, usually well above what a package like the Wedding Pack costs. For most Malaga weddings under 80 guests, that level of customization is more than the day needs. The Wedding Pack sits between doing it yourself and hiring a full production house: professional gear and a technician, at a fixed price, sized for a typical wedding rather than a large scale production.

If damage protection or liability terms matter to how you weigh renting against buying or hiring, we do not publish a policy for either path. See our [protecting your wedding rental items](/blog/protecting-your-wedding-rental-items/) guide for exactly what MEG does and does not commit to on that front.

